Do not keep geodata that no rule uses.

mihomo verifies GeoSite.dat and GeoIP.dat the first time a GEOSITE or GEOIP
rule appears, and it does so by loading the CN list. The result lands in the
same caches as real rules, so every process with a geo rule kept a CN matcher
it never matches against. On top of that each loaded geosite code was held
twice: the raw domain list and the matcher built from it, although only the
matcher is ever used after loading.

Both caches are fixed here. Verify still loads CN -- that is the check -- and
then forgets it; a rule that really asks for CN loads it again. The raw list is
no longer stored; the only cost is a second scan of the file when one config
uses the same code with different @attributes.

Measured on Windows against the same build without this patch (working set,
the core with no geo rules at all is 19.6 MB):

    GEOSITE category-ru only                      22.5-23.0 -> 21.6-21.9 MB
    category-ru + category-ads-all + GEOIP ru     24.8-25.8 -> 22.5-22.6 MB
    + geolocation-!cn (25 000 entries)            28.7-31.0 -> 23.9-25.7 MB

Routing decisions for GeoSite(cn), GeoSite(category-*), GeoIP(ru) and MATCH
were compared on both builds and are identical.

Rebase check: keep the Forget keys in step with how LoadGeoSiteMatcher and
LoadGeoIPMatcher build their cache keys (lower-cased list name, no attributes).

